@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# UGV Simulator Dependency Matrix
+
+This is the qualification handoff. No listed dependency was observed in this Goal; deterministic fixtures are not simulator authority.
+
+| Provider capability   | Device MCP requirement                                                                                                                 | MQTT/Observation requirement                                                                                                                                                          | Correlation requirement                                                                             | Physical qualification                                                                                                        | Status                                                     |
+| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
+| State                 | `get_status`: online, identity, task states, speed, payload/health                                                                     | `status/ugv`, `/ugv/system_state`, `/ugv/component_status`, `/ugv/battery_range_km`                                                                                                   | entity identity and source sequence/time                                                            | none; compare MCP/MQTT consistency                                                                                            | PENDING_SIMULATOR_CONTRACT + PENDING_SIMULATOR_OBSERVATION |
+| Capabilities          | `get_capabilities`: supported operations/limits, no guessed engineering values                                                         | optional capability/state topic if provided                                                                                                                                           | vehicle identity and contract revision                                                              | none                                                                                                                          | PENDING_SIMULATOR_CONTRACT                                 |
+| Payload/targets/range | optional `ugv_area_recon_get_targets`, `ugv_laser_range`                                                                               | `/ugv/area_recon/targets`, `/ugv/detected_objects`; target id/type/position/time/sequence                                                                                             | target id and observation authority                                                                 | controlled target/range fixtures                                                                                              | PENDING_SIMULATOR_CONTRACT + PENDING_SIMULATOR_OBSERVATION |
+| Navigate              | `ugv_move_distance` or `ugv_path_follow_mission`; `ugv_mission_control`; result mission id                                             | `/ugv/gnss`, `/ugv/speed`, `/ugv/mission_state`, `/ugv/nav_state`, `status/ugv`; lat/lon/alt, heading, speed, state, progress, mission id, source time/sequence                       | returned mission id must match terminal observations; ordering must be newer than dispatch baseline | point and distance missions, stale/duplicate/reordered samples, stationary completion and independently measured displacement | PENDING_SIMULATOR_PHYSICAL_QUALIFICATION                   |
+| Pause/Resume/Cancel   | `ugv_mission_control` actions and mission id                                                                                           | mission state plus fresh speed and source ordering                                                                                                                                    | same mission id across command and observations                                                     | ACK/state separation, delayed state, pause stationary, resume active while stationary, cancel stationary                      | PENDING_SIMULATOR_PHYSICAL_QUALIFICATION                   |
+| Emergency stop        | `ugv_motion_stop`; unambiguous accepted/uncertain result                                                                               | new `/ugv/speed`, mission/recon/weapon/EO task states and target-lock status                                                                                                          | all facts later than stop baseline and for configured entity                                        | moving vehicle stop latency; missing/stale speed; active recon/lock; no automatic replay after timeout                        | PENDING_SIMULATOR_PHYSICAL_QUALIFICATION                   |
+| Area recon            | `ugv_area_recon_configure`, `ugv_area_recon_control`, `ugv_area_recon_get_status`, `ugv_area_recon_get_targets`; result mission/run id | `/ugv/area_recon/status`, `/targets`, `/coverage`, `/exception`; id, scan mode, progress, coverage, coverability, motion status, fault, out-of-range, exception, source time/sequence | mission/run id when present; otherwise explicitly weak, never invented                              | start/progress/terminal/fault/out-of-range/cancel and target observations                                                     | PENDING_SIMULATOR_PHYSICAL_QUALIFICATION                   |
+| Track target          | optional downstream tracking tool and target id                                                                                        | target/EO tracking state, lock id, source authority                                                                                                                                   | target id and task/mission id                                                                       | acquire/loss/cancel                                                                                                           | PENDING_SIMULATOR_CONTRACT                                 |
+| Gimbal                | optional gimbal-control tool with supported axes/ranges                                                                                | gimbal position/state and source authority                                                                                                                                            | configured vehicle and command sequence                                                             | bounded movement and terminal position                                                                                        | PENDING_SIMULATOR_CONTRACT                                 |
+| Fire                  | historical fire tools may be captured read-only, but Provider gate remains disabled                                                    | weapon/lock state may be observed read-only                                                                                                                                           | no physical fire task may be created                                                                | real fire is forbidden in this Goal                                                                                           | PENDING_SIMULATOR_CONTRACT; DISABLED_BY_POLICY             |
+
+## Wire-level capture requirements
+
+- Capture `tools/list` names, descriptions, input schemas and output/result schemas for every required and optional tool.
+- Capture success, business rejection, malformed result, timeout-after-dispatch, disconnect, reconnect and circuit recovery behavior.
+- For every MQTT topic record broker URL class (redacted), wire mode, QoS, retained flag, payload bytes, decoded field names/types/units, frequency, source timestamp, source sequence/revision, reconnect/reset semantics and configured entity identity.
+- Required topics: `status/ugv`, `/ugv/gnss`, `/ugv/speed`, `/ugv/mission_state`, `/ugv/nav_state`, `/ugv/system_state`, `/ugv/component_status`, `/ugv/battery_range_km`, `/ugv/area_recon/status`, `/ugv/area_recon/targets`, `/ugv/area_recon/coverage`, `/ugv/area_recon/exception`.
+- Qualification must explicitly distinguish source-authoritative ordering from the weaker ingest-order fallback.
+
+## Physical scenario inputs
+
+1. Point navigation with known start/end coordinates and independently measurable displacement.
+2. Distance navigation with requested distance, speed limit, stationary completion and tolerance evaluated outside Provider.
+3. Duplicate, stale and reordered mission/position/speed packets around terminal state.
+4. Pause ACK before physical pause, Resume while stationary/planning, Cancel followed by fresh stop.
+5. Emergency stop while moving, while recon is active, while target locked, and with missing/stale speed.
+6. Recon normal completion, empty target set, fault, out-of-range, exception, lost/missing correlation and cancel.
+7. MCP read disconnect/retry recovery and mutating timeout with observation-only reconciliation.
+
+## Deferred roadmap dependencies
+
+- Component power: command/state contract and component inventory.
+- Precise turn: angle/radius command plus heading/trajectory evidence.
+- Payload brightness/focus/absolute zoom: command ranges and state feedback.
+- Media capture: image/video/stream contract and Artifact service integration.
+- Static engineering profile: minimum turning radius, maximum grade, obstacle height, nominal detection range and physical dimensions from engineering authority.
